This repository includes demo audio whose speaker references are derived from
the JVS corpus:

  S. Takamichi, K. Mitsui, Y. Saito, T. Koriyama, N. Tanji, and H. Saruwatari,
  "JVS corpus: free Japanese multi-speaker voice corpus," arXiv:1908.06248, 2019.
  https://sites.google.com/site/shinnosuketakamichi/research-topics/jvs_corpus

JVS-derived audio is available for academic / non-commercial research and
personal use only, and is NOT covered by the Apache License 2.0 of this
repository. See docs/LICENSE-audio.md.

The bundled G2P dictionary (assets/g2p/japanese_mfa.dict) is an unmodified copy of
the Montreal Forced Aligner "japanese_mfa" dictionary v3.0.0 by Michael McAuliffe
and Morgan Sonderegger (2024), distributed under CC BY 4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).

  Upstream: https://github.com/MontrealCorpusTools/mfa-models/releases/tag/dictionary-japanese_mfa-v3.0.0
  Docs:     https://mfa-models.readthedocs.io/

  The bundled file is byte-identical to the released japanese_mfa.dict
  (SHA-256 4a0c66760576e4b7f3748f3169e7d5217c0135f857f0b5d34637c93a85fd1c91);
  no changes were made. It is the probabilistic variant of the dictionary, which
  carries the pronunciation and silence probabilities published upstream.

Synthesis downloads the Semantic-DACVAE-Japanese-32dim weights (MIT License) at
run time; they are not redistributed here. The DACVAE code installed as a
dependency is licensed under Apache License 2.0.

The acoustic model is derived from Irodori-TTS-500M-v2 (MIT License) and the
text converter from llm-jp/llm-jp-3-440m (Apache License 2.0).

This repository vendors the irodori_tts package from Irodori-TTS
(https://github.com/Aratako/Irodori-TTS, commit 2708d3c, MIT License, unmodified).
The bundled training config assets/irodori_train_500m_v2.yaml is likewise an
unmodified copy of configs/train_500m_v2.yaml from the same commit and is covered
by the same MIT License. See irodori_tts/LICENSE.
